#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:59
#: b3c25590a9574e51b233407ec1c53da5
msgid "Variants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:61
#: 9e071f9781694903bf882a4d5a35b3c0
msgid "In addition to STD and CTR versions, there are older variants called -AIO and -OSD that have been declared end-of-life by Mateksys.  Both use the ICM20602 IMU, like the STD version. Neither have an onboard barometer. While the -AIO has I2C pads exposed, the -OSD version does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:65
#: 5fe26ec7cd6f453ebbb917e6f39455e5
msgid "For the -STD version please use the MatekF405-STD type firmware. For the -CTR version with MPU6000 please use the MatekF405 type firmware. For the :ref:`MatekF405-Wing <common-matekf405-wing>` which has an essentially different board layout please use the dedicated firmware. Please note that ArduPilot does not support -AIO and -OSD versions per default as additional hardware and / or software adjustments are required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:67
#: 470a7ce4da1248b88ff3c4b6b1db3240
msgid "The MatekF405-CTR has a firmware version supporting :ref:`bi-directional Dshot <bidir-dshot>` labeled \"MatekF405-bdshot\". Note this is only supported for outputs 1-4 in this version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:71
#: eb5217fdfb5d4770a0ea4d5352afb0e6
msgid "Default UART order"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:73
#: 24ace2f1fb50423a8ecd41c948f4a70d
msgid "SERIAL0 = console = USB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:74
#: 851c14df2142405fbc0e00cb82aca7ad
msgid "SERIAL1 = Telemetry1 = USART3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:75
#: 426027ddd71a49ca84b48d3f756949f7
msgid "SERIAL2 = Telemetry2 = UART4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:76
#: 9d384390ef2e47bda2fd3c57a49b4521
msgid "SERIAL3 = GPS1 = USART1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:77
#: 491b8d484495443fa047214c32a21395
msgid "SERIAL4 = GPS2 = UART5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:78
#: 7f83534c0a0d4cd2a227e3ed5183ce68
msgid "SERIAL5 = User = USART2 (TX only unless :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` = 1, then RX is available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:80
#: c9f956bfacc446a5999ec70a45b61ab2
msgid "Serial protocols can be adjusted to personal preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:83
#: 9ffa1dfccb7d42ffbfa60b2e2ac67a06
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:85
#: a36406fc488f41fab33504e51fcdbe93
msgid "The SBUS pin, is passed by an inverter to R2 (UART2 RX), which by default is mapped to a timer input instead of the UART, and can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, will only provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:87
#: b5cc6ce3126544898e3515d993f9ff82
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, the R2 pin can also be configured to be used as true UART2 RX pin for use with bi-directional systems by setting the :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` to “1” so it becomes the SERIAL5 port's RX input pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:89
#: 740d6f77b6264a22bc3d1c8ad16e32cc
msgid "With this option, :ref:`SERIAL5_PROTOCOL<SERIAL5_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\", and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:91
#: 2810772f2cef49209b0215e028dd2c84
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:93
#: db38764210c8439c856fb291b2f58cd2
msgid "DSM/SRXL connects to the R2  pin, but SBUS would still be connected to SBUS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:95
#: 17d66b67d21343ea867db1a4e5bddbcc
msgid "FPort requires connection to T2 and R2 via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:97
#: 88a167fc6cbc486f8b7310c49f70fbe2
msgid "CRSF also requires a T2 connection, in addition to R2, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:99
#: 82a9978d581b4e89b8f7f163ccb82acf
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to T2 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:101
#: 90b087a37bbe4c49a477c9ce010b9ee0
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM (SBUS requires external inversion on other UARTs). See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:104
#: 244b6ce6e5724991a9ef3fcc9d97b691
msgid "Dshot capability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-matekf405.rst:106
#: afe9ca9c89074a82a87e04779a5a6bb6
msgid "All motor/servo outputs are Dshot and PWM capable. However, mixing Dshot and normal PWM operation for outputs is restricted into groups, ie. enabling Dshot for an output in a group requires that ALL outputs in that group be configured and used as Dshot, rather than PWM outputs. The output groups that must be the same (PWM rate or Dshot, when configured as a normal servo/motor output) are: 1, 2/3/4, 5, 6, and 7 (-STD only)."
msgstr ""

